  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, I checked your laptop (BL-LT-0101). It is online and reports about 310 GB free on its 512 GB drive, which is roughly 60% free, and it shows no disk warnings. That means the low disk space message may be out of date, or it may refer to a different drive or partition. Could you send me the exact wording of the warning, the drive letter it names if any, and roughly when it appeared? If you still see it, restart the laptop and tell me whether it comes back. If you would like to free up space yourself, go to Settings > System > Storage > Temporary files and empty the Recycle Bin and Downloads folder. I have not changed anything on your laptop.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user for dana.whitfield (user_id 1, CEO, VIP, active, not blocked). Device BL-LT-0101 (Windows 11 Pro) is online, last check-in 2026-10-11 03:25 UTC. Disk: 512 GB total, 310 GB free, percent_free 60.5%, no warnings. KB-017 threshold (under 10% free) is not met, so the cleanup/escalation path does not apply. No cleanup was run remotely; no action tools were used. Likely a stale Windows notification or a warning for another volume. Asked user for exact warning text, drive letter, and timing. If the user reports a warning on a specific volume, re-check that volume or the device before proceeding. Mailbox is 17.4% used (not a factor).",
